    "_meanings": [
        ".²1 <ab>N.</ab> of the king of birds. [He is a son of Kaśyapa by his wife Vinatā.\n He is the chief of the feathered race, an implacable enemy of serpents,\n and elder brother of Aruṇa. In a dispute between his mother and Kadrū,\n her rival, about the colour of {#ucEHSravas#} Kadrū defeated Vinatā,\n and, in accordance with the conditions of the wager, made her her slave.\n Garuḍa brought down the heavenly beverage (Amṛta) to purchase her freedom,\n not, however, without a hard struggle with Indra for the same. Vinatā\n was then released; but the Amṛta was taken away by Indra from the serpents.\n Garuḍa is represented as the vehicle of Viṣṇu, and as having a white\n face, an aquiline nose, red wings and a golden body.]\n",
        ".²2 A building or architecture (such as {#citi#}) shaped like Garuḍa;\n {#garuqo rukmapakzo vE triguRo'zwAdaSAtmakaH#} <ls>Rām. 1. 14. 29</ls>.\n",
        ".²3 <ab>N.</ab> of a particular military array.\n"
    ],
